  message: "DONE in PR #2194 (dev 009dde0116, manifest 3c648fa193), on the owner's go of 2026-11-15. An import inside a function body is an edge only in a file outside the source roots; in a source module an import counts when it runs as the module loads (module level, class body, under try or if there, a decorator, a parameter default). EVIDENCE, each DONE WHEN: (1) repro: STABLE_ID_SCHEME edited in schema.py, scripts/smart-test --manifest exits 0 and the manifest holds packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_shape_ids.py. (2) that manifest has 514 test files, 202 of them this branch's own selection; the shipped rule gave 1,414. schema.py's closure by a static call: 314 test files (1,423 before). (3) mikag_cost_11142026/real_cost.py re-run with the built module (the merge was a rebase, same file): selected test time 232,518 to 255,232 test seconds (+9.8%; was +25.3%), 44 of 90 PRs select more, median share of the suite 52% to 56%; that figure is in ADR-0010 and the module docstring. (4) the bed and the unit tests pass slicing with hypergumbo 9.0.0 and with the tree's 9.2.0 build (130 passed each); mutation controls: counting function-level imports everywhere gives 13 failures (12 unit cases and the bed), counting them nowhere gives 53 (52 unit cases and the bed). (5) ADR-0010 states the known miss, and tests/test_smart_test_bed.py asserts it (test_reads_lazily.py is MUST and not in the manifest). The graph equals the lab variant's on the tree of 2026-11-15 (0 of 1,912 files differ; 236 edges fewer than shipped, in 78 source files), so the decorator and parameter-default cases change no edge here. NOT MEASURED: how many test files of this repository reach some change only through a function-level import in a source module. Evidence files: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nusil_11152026/."  # bb41
